From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:05:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iio: aop_als: make the calibration blob optional

The ambient light sensor's calibration blob (apple/aop-als-cal.bin) is
extracted from macOS and is not installed on every system. Without it
the driver fails to probe, although the sensor reports without it, only
uncalibrated (seen on the M4 Pro as on earlier machines).

Load the blob when present; otherwise warn that the readings are
uncalibrated and carry on. The CT817 path, which gets its calibration
over the setup port, is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs b/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
index 3047fd7ba5..4cbd1e2846 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
@@ -101,8 +101,18 @@ fn enable_als(
     offset: usize,
 ) -> Result<()> {
     if offset != LUX_OFFSET_CT817 {
-        let fw = Firmware::request(c_str!("apple/aop-als-cal.bin"), dev.as_ref())?;
-        set_als_property(aop, svc, ALS_PROP_CALIBRATION, fw.data())?;
+        // The calibration blob comes from macOS and is not installed on every
+        // system. Without it the sensor still reports, uncalibrated.
+        match Firmware::request(c_str!("apple/aop-als-cal.bin"), dev.as_ref()) {
+            Ok(fw) => {
+                set_als_property(aop, svc, ALS_PROP_CALIBRATION, fw.data())?;
+            }
+            Err(e) => dev_warn!(
+                dev.as_ref(),
+                "no calibration ({:?}); readings are uncalibrated\n",
+                e
+            ),
+        }
         set_als_property(aop, svc, ALS_PROP_INTERVAL, &ALS_INTERVAL_US.to_le_bytes())?;
         return Ok(());
     }
